# Literal coordinates for the second J₄ seed centralizer

The columns of `adaptedRows` are the first independent columns of `t - 1`,
followed by their standard-coordinate preimages. The 56 algebra words are
the displayed echelon basis in the seed algebra witness. Bit `56*i+j` of
an algebra word is matrix entry `(i,j)`. These are data, not rank assertions.

Reproduced from `Scratch/J4FleetGuidance/SeedCentralizer/explore.py` and
`witnesses.json` in the source workspace; the script reads the ATLAS matrices
documented in `Janko4.Model.Data`. The companion coordinate module certifies
the inverse, seed normal form, and invariant-pairing calibration in Lean.
-/

